+-- W0-10 PR-4b · make rigs.operatorId NULLABLE (column KEPT; dropped in PR-4c).
+-- Expand/contract, middle phase: this revision REMOVES the operatorId/assignedOperatorId/
+-- RigOperator fields from schema.prisma, so the generated Prisma client stops projecting
+-- (reading) and stops writing those columns — but the DB columns still physically exist.
+-- Relaxing NOT NULL lets rig.create (which no longer supplies operatorId) insert NULL while
+-- the column remains. Additive/backward-compatible; DROP NOT NULL is not in the CI
+-- migration-safety denylist. After this deploys, the live revision neither reads NOR writes
+-- the legacy columns (client no longer references them) -> PR-4c's DROP is fully gap-safe.
+ALTER TABLE "rigs" ALTER COLUMN "operatorId" DROP NOT NULL;
